                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ca8127de-0b6a-3fbf-a3c8-dd7387ae10e8",
                                        "entry_id": "ce5c9c64-4603-31df-8ab8-76d22fb3d947",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The god of volcanoes and fire, especially the forge, also the patron of all craftsmen, especially blacksmiths. The Roman counterpart of Hephaestus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "Roman"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4edc8015-ffd5-418e-aaf3-1b47a56d5c15",
                                                "sense_id": "ca8127de-0b6a-3fbf-a3c8-dd7387ae10e8",
                                                "text": "The goddess Venus was the wife of Vulcan."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "14470dad-27fb-44c2-8b52-94dd52c6b349",
                                                "sense_id": "ca8127de-0b6a-3fbf-a3c8-dd7387ae10e8",
                                                "text": "But I perceiue nowe that all red colloured stones are not Rubies, nether is euery one Alexander that hath a stare in his cheke, al lame men are not Vulcans, nor hooke nosed men Ciceroes, nether each professor a poet."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e6b2a86d-750d-3c62-aa84-3f0bf6ffae6c",
